[{"input":"# Lecture 8 – Computer Networks and the Internet \n\n## Learning Objectives \n\nAt the end of this chapter, students should be able to: \n\n- Explain why computer networks exist. \n\n- Distinguish between local networks and the Internet. \n\n- Understand the concepts of protocols, packets, clients, and servers. \n\n- Explain the roles of IP, TCP, UDP, and DNS. \n\n- Understand how information travels across the Internet. \n\n- Describe how websites are accessed. \n\n- Understand the concepts of cloud computing and online services. \n\n- Follow the complete journey of a web request. ","output":"","result":"# Lecture 8 – Computer Networks and the Internet \n\n## Learning Objectives \n\nAt the end of this chapter, students should be able to: \n\n- Explain why computer networks exist. \n\n- Distinguish between local networks and the Internet. \n\n- Understand the concepts of protocols, packets, clients, and servers. \n\n- Explain the roles of IP, TCP, UDP, and DNS. \n\n- Understand how information travels across the Internet. \n\n- Describe how websites are accessed. \n\n- Understand the concepts of cloud computing and online services. \n\n- Follow the complete journey of a web request. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"chapter\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3469-lecture-8-computer-networks-and-the-internet\">\n<h1>Lecture 8 – Computer Networks and the Internet</h1>\n<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3469-learning-objectives\">\n<h1>Learning Objectives</h1>\n<p>At the end of this chapter, students should be able to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Explain why computer networks exist.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Distinguish between local networks and the Internet.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Understand the concepts of protocols, packets, clients, and servers.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Explain the roles of IP, TCP, UDP, and DNS.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Understand how information travels across the Internet.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Describe how websites are accessed.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Understand the concepts of cloud computing and online services.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Follow the complete journey of a web request.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"76a648cd74a741f9e34106adf57ca725357eb4d4253152b8fcac7a82d3d56d1c","markdown":"# Les 8 – Computernetwerken en het Internet \n\n## Leerdoelen \n\nAan het einde van dit hoofdstuk moeten studenten in staat zijn om: \n\n- Uit te leggen waarom computernetwerken bestaan. \n\n- Een onderscheid te maken tussen lokale netwerken en het Internet. \n\n- De concepten protocollen, pakketten, clients en servers te begrijpen. \n\n- De rollen van IP, TCP, UDP en DNS uit te leggen. \n\n- Te begrijpen hoe informatie over het Internet reist. \n\n- Te beschrijven hoe websites worden benaderd. \n\n- De concepten cloud computing en online diensten te begrijpen. \n\n- De volledige reis van een webverzoek te volgen."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"76a648cd74a741f9e34106adf57ca725357eb4d4253152b8fcac7a82d3d56d1c","markdown":"# Cours 8 – Réseaux informatiques et Internet \n\n## Objectifs d'apprentissage \n\nÀ la fin de ce chapitre, les étudiants devraient être capables de : \n\n- Expliquer pourquoi les réseaux informatiques existent. \n\n- Distinguer les réseaux locaux d'Internet. \n\n- Comprendre les concepts de protocoles, de paquets, de clients et de serveurs. \n\n- Expliquer les rôles de l'IP, du TCP, de l'UDP et du DNS. \n\n- Comprendre comment l'information circule sur Internet. \n\n- Décrire comment les sites web sont accessibles. \n\n- Comprendre les concepts d'informatique en nuage et de services en ligne. \n\n- Suivre le parcours complet d'une requête web."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"76a648cd74a741f9e34106adf57ca725357eb4d4253152b8fcac7a82d3d56d1c","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Introduction \n\nSo far, we have studied a single computer: \n\n- Hardware \n\n- Software \n\n- Operating systems \n\nHowever, modern computing is rarely performed in isolation. \n\nMost applications depend on communication between computers. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Viewing websites \n\n- Sending emails \n\n- Streaming videos \n\n- Online gaming \n\n- Social media \n\n- Cloud storage \n\n- Artificial intelligence services \n\nThis communication is enabled by computer networks. ","output":"","result":"## Introduction \n\nSo far, we have studied a single computer: \n\n- Hardware \n\n- Software \n\n- Operating systems \n\nHowever, modern computing is rarely performed in isolation. \n\nMost applications depend on communication between computers. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Viewing websites \n\n- Sending emails \n\n- Streaming videos \n\n- Online gaming \n\n- Social media \n\n- Cloud storage \n\n- Artificial intelligence services \n\nThis communication is enabled by computer networks. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3471-introduction\">\n<h1>Introduction</h1>\n<p>So far, we have studied a single computer:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Hardware</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Software</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Operating systems</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>However, modern computing is rarely performed in isolation.</p>\n<p>Most applications depend on communication between computers.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Viewing websites</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Sending emails</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Streaming videos</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Online gaming</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Social media</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Cloud storage</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Artificial intelligence services</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This communication is enabled by computer networks.</p>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"9870951635f457279aeefd3f43d5ac27f48eb22ff4d098370695093e17b58ef4","markdown":"## Inleiding \n\nTot nu toe hebben we een enkele computer bestudeerd: \n\n- Hardware \n\n- Software \n\n- Besturingssystemen \n\nModern computergebruik vindt echter zelden geïsoleerd plaats. \n\nDe meeste toepassingen zijn afhankelijk van communicatie tussen computers. \n\nVoorbeelden: \n\n- Websites bekijken \n\n- E-mails verzenden \n\n- Video's streamen \n\n- Online gamen \n\n- Sociale media \n\n- Cloudopslag \n\n- Diensten voor kunstmatige intelligentie \n\nDeze communicatie wordt mogelijk gemaakt door computernetwerken. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"9870951635f457279aeefd3f43d5ac27f48eb22ff4d098370695093e17b58ef4","markdown":"## Introduction \n\nJusqu'à présent, nous avons étudié un seul ordinateur : \n\n- Matériel \n\n- Logiciel \n\n- Systèmes d'exploitation \n\nCependant, l'informatique moderne est rarement réalisée de manière isolée. \n\nLa plupart des applications dépendent de la communication entre ordinateurs. \n\nExemples : \n\n- Consulter des sites web \n\n- Envoyer des courriels \n\n- Diffuser des vidéos en continu \n\n- Jeux en ligne \n\n- Médias sociaux \n\n- Stockage en nuage \n\n- Services d'intelligence artificielle \n\nCette communication est rendue possible par les réseaux informatiques. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"9870951635f457279aeefd3f43d5ac27f48eb22ff4d098370695093e17b58ef4","language":"English"}},{"input":"## What Is a Network? \n\nA network is a collection of devices that can communicate and exchange information. \n\nExamples of devices include: \n\n- Computers \n\n- Smartphones \n\n- Printers \n\n- Servers \n\n- Routers \n\n- Smart TVs \n\n### Everyday Example \n\nAt home you may have: \n```text\n Laptop \n Smartphone \n Printer \n Smart TV\n```\n\nall connected to the same network. \n\nThis allows them to exchange information. \n\n### Benefits of Networks \n\nNetworks allow devices to: \n\n- Share information \n\n- Share resources \n\n- Communicate efficiently \n\n- Access remote services \n\nWithout networks, every computer would operate independently. ","output":"","result":"## What Is a Network? \n\nA network is a collection of devices that can communicate and exchange information. \n\nExamples of devices include: \n\n- Computers \n\n- Smartphones \n\n- Printers \n\n- Servers \n\n- Routers \n\n- Smart TVs \n\n### Everyday Example \n\nAt home you may have: \n```text\n Laptop \n Smartphone \n Printer \n Smart TV\n```\n\nall connected to the same network. \n\nThis allows them to exchange information. \n\n### Benefits of Networks \n\nNetworks allow devices to: \n\n- Share information \n\n- Share resources \n\n- Communicate efficiently \n\n- Access remote services \n\nWithout networks, every computer would operate independently. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3472-what-is-a-network\">\n<h1>What Is a Network?</h1>\n<p>A network is a collection of devices that can communicate and exchange information.</p>\n<p>Examples of devices include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Computers</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Smartphones</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Printers</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Servers</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Routers</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Smart TVs</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3472-everyday-example\">\n<h1>Everyday Example</h1>\n<p>At home you may have:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\"> Laptop \n Smartphone \n Printer \n Smart TV</pre>\n<p>all connected to the same network.</p>\n<p>This allows them to exchange information.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3472-benefits-of-networks\">\n<h1>Benefits of Networks</h1>\n<p>Networks allow devices to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Share information</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Share resources</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Communicate efficiently</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Access remote services</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Without networks, every computer would operate independently.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"9fa3acec3c93816baf1f33907b374f662eb8415792516789e89b54f2f703faf9","markdown":"## Wat Is een Netwerk? \n\nEen netwerk is een verzameling apparaten die kunnen communiceren en informatie kunnen uitwisselen. \n\nVoorbeelden van apparaten zijn: \n\n- Computers \n\n- Smartphones \n\n- Printers \n\n- Servers \n\n- Routers \n\n- Smart-tv's \n\n### Alledaags Voorbeeld \n\nThuis heb je misschien: \n```text\n Laptop \n Smartphone \n Printer \n Smart TV\n```\n\nallemaal verbonden met hetzelfde netwerk. \n\nHierdoor kunnen ze informatie uitwisselen. \n\n### Voordelen van Netwerken \n\nNetwerken stellen apparaten in staat om: \n\n- Informatie te delen \n\n- Bronnen te delen \n\n- Efficiënt te communiceren \n\n- Toegang te krijgen tot externe diensten \n\nZonder netwerken zou elke computer onafhankelijk werken. \n"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"9fa3acec3c93816baf1f33907b374f662eb8415792516789e89b54f2f703faf9","markdown":"## Qu'est-ce qu'un réseau ?\n\nUn réseau est un ensemble d'appareils capables de communiquer et d'échanger des informations.\n\nExemples d'appareils :\n\n- Ordinateurs\n\n- Smartphones\n\n- Imprimantes\n\n- Serveurs\n\n- Routeurs\n\n- Téléviseurs connectés\n\n### Exemple du quotidien\n\nChez vous, vous pouvez avoir :\n```text\n Laptop \n Smartphone \n Printer \n Smart TV\n```\n\ntous connectés au même réseau.\n\nCela leur permet d'échanger des informations.\n\n### Avantages des réseaux\n\nLes réseaux permettent aux appareils de :\n\n- Partager des informations\n\n- Partager des ressources\n\n- Communiquer efficacement\n\n- Accéder à des services distants\n\nSans réseaux, chaque ordinateur fonctionnerait de manière indépendante."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"9fa3acec3c93816baf1f33907b374f662eb8415792516789e89b54f2f703faf9","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Local Networks and the Internet \n\n### Local Area Network (LAN) \n\nA Local Area Network connects devices within a limited area. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Home network \n\n- School network \n\n- Office network \n\n \n\n#### Example \n\n```text\n     Laptop \n        │ \n     Router \n        │ \n     Printer \n```\n\nAll devices communicate locally. \n\n\n### Internet \n\nThe Internet is a global network connecting millions of smaller networks. \n\nRather than being a single computer, the Internet is: \n\n```text\n     Network \n     connected to \n     Network \n     connected to \n     Network \n     ... \n```\n\non a worldwide scale. \n\n \n\n### Important Distinction \n\n#### LAN \n\n```text\n     Small Area \n     Private\n```\n\n#### Internet \n\n```text\n     Global \n     Public \n```","output":"","result":"## Local Networks and the Internet \n\n### Local Area Network (LAN) \n\nA Local Area Network connects devices within a limited area. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Home network \n\n- School network \n\n- Office network \n\n \n\n#### Example \n\n```text\n     Laptop \n        │ \n     Router \n        │ \n     Printer \n```\n\nAll devices communicate locally. \n\n\n### Internet \n\nThe Internet is a global network connecting millions of smaller networks. \n\nRather than being a single computer, the Internet is: \n\n```text\n     Network \n     connected to \n     Network \n     connected to \n     Network \n     ... \n```\n\non a worldwide scale. \n\n \n\n### Important Distinction \n\n#### LAN \n\n```text\n     Small Area \n     Private\n```\n\n#### Internet \n\n```text\n     Global \n     Public \n```","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3473-local-networks-and-the-internet\">\n<h1>Local Networks and the Internet</h1>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3473-local-area-network-lan\">\n<h1>Local Area Network (LAN)</h1>\n<p>A Local Area Network connects devices within a limited area.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Home network</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>School network</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Office network</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<section data-type=\"sect3\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3473-example\">\n<h1>Example</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Laptop \n        │ \n     Router \n        │ \n     Printer </pre>\n<p>All devices communicate locally.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3473-internet\">\n<h1>Internet</h1>\n<p>The Internet is a global network connecting millions of smaller networks.</p>\n<p>Rather than being a single computer, the Internet is:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Network \n     connected to \n     Network \n     connected to \n     Network \n     ... </pre>\n<p>on a worldwide scale.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3473-important-distinction\">\n<h1>Important Distinction</h1>\n<section data-type=\"sect3\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3473-lan\">\n<h1>LAN</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Small Area \n     Private</pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect3\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3473-internet-2\">\n<h1>Internet</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Global \n     Public </pre>\n</section>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"0b0969898a32a333d1488cf51748177e63dcce8c73524966ae77b80eca0eb72e","markdown":"## Lokale Netwerken en het Internet \n\n### Local Area Network (LAN) \n\nEen Local Area Network verbindt apparaten binnen een beperkt gebied. \n\nVoorbeelden: \n\n- Thuisnetwerk \n\n- Schoolnetwerk \n\n- Kantoornetwerk \n\n \n\n#### Voorbeeld \n\n```text\n     Laptop \n        │ \n     Router \n        │ \n     Printer \n```\n\nAlle apparaten communiceren lokaal. \n\n\n### Internet \n\nHet internet is een wereldwijd netwerk dat miljoenen kleinere netwerken met elkaar verbindt. \n\nIn plaats van één enkele computer, is het internet: \n\n```text\n     Network \n     connected to \n     Network \n     connected to \n     Network \n     ... \n```\n\nop wereldwijde schaal. \n\n \n\n### Belangrijk Onderscheid \n\n#### LAN \n\n```text\n     Small Area \n     Private\n```\n\n#### Internet \n\n```text\n     Global \n     Public \n```"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"0b0969898a32a333d1488cf51748177e63dcce8c73524966ae77b80eca0eb72e","markdown":"## Réseaux locaux et Internet \n\n### Réseau local (LAN) \n\nUn réseau local connecte des appareils à l'intérieur d'une zone limitée. \n\nExemples : \n\n- Réseau domestique \n\n- Réseau scolaire \n\n- Réseau de bureau \n\n \n\n#### Exemple \n\n```text\n     Laptop \n        │ \n     Router \n        │ \n     Printer \n```\n\nTous les appareils communiquent localement. \n\n\n### Internet \n\nInternet est un réseau mondial qui connecte des millions de réseaux plus petits. \n\nPlutôt qu'un ordinateur unique, Internet est : \n\n```text\n     Network \n     connected to \n     Network \n     connected to \n     Network \n     ... \n```\n\nà l'échelle mondiale. \n\n \n\n### Distinction importante \n\n#### LAN \n\n```text\n     Small Area \n     Private\n```\n\n#### Internet \n\n```text\n     Global \n     Public \n```"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"0b0969898a32a333d1488cf51748177e63dcce8c73524966ae77b80eca0eb72e","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Communication Requires Rules \n\nImagine a conversation where everyone uses different languages. \n\nCommunication would be difficult. \n\nComputers face the same challenge. \n\nThey need common rules. \n\n### Protocols \n\nA protocol is a set of rules that define how communication occurs. \n\nProtocols specify: \n\n- Message format \n\n- Transmission methods \n\n- Error handling \n\n- Interpretation of information \n\n \n\n### Everyday Analogy \n\nHuman communication relies on rules. \n\nFor example: \n\n```text\n     One person speaks. \n     The other listens. \n```\n\nComputer communication also requires agreed-upon procedures. ","output":"","result":"## Communication Requires Rules \n\nImagine a conversation where everyone uses different languages. \n\nCommunication would be difficult. \n\nComputers face the same challenge. \n\nThey need common rules. \n\n### Protocols \n\nA protocol is a set of rules that define how communication occurs. \n\nProtocols specify: \n\n- Message format \n\n- Transmission methods \n\n- Error handling \n\n- Interpretation of information \n\n \n\n### Everyday Analogy \n\nHuman communication relies on rules. \n\nFor example: \n\n```text\n     One person speaks. \n     The other listens. \n```\n\nComputer communication also requires agreed-upon procedures. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3474-communication-requires-rules\">\n<h1>Communication Requires Rules</h1>\n<p>Imagine a conversation where everyone uses different languages.</p>\n<p>Communication would be difficult.</p>\n<p>Computers face the same challenge.</p>\n<p>They need common rules.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3474-protocols\">\n<h1>Protocols</h1>\n<p>A protocol is a set of rules that define how communication occurs.</p>\n<p>Protocols specify:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Message format</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Transmission methods</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Error handling</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Interpretation of information</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3474-everyday-analogy\">\n<h1>Everyday Analogy</h1>\n<p>Human communication relies on rules.</p>\n<p>For example:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     One person speaks. \n     The other listens. </pre>\n<p>Computer communication also requires agreed-upon procedures.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"eaf8caac81a6b4ef721e5362cf483e39f879a92c8ae3e847ec8c3af50ec9eb0f","markdown":"## Communicatie Vereist Regels \n\nStel je een gesprek voor waarin iedereen een andere taal spreekt. \n\nCommunicatie zou moeilijk zijn. \n\nComputers worden met dezelfde uitdaging geconfronteerd. \n\nZe hebben gemeenschappelijke regels nodig. \n\n### Protocollen \n\nEen protocol is een set regels die bepaalt hoe communicatie plaatsvindt. \n\nProtocollen specificeren: \n\n- Berichtformaat \n\n- Transmissiemethoden \n\n- Foutafhandeling \n\n- Interpretatie van informatie \n\n \n\n### Alledaagse Analogie \n\nMenselijke communicatie steunt op regels. \n\nBijvoorbeeld: \n\n```text\n     One person speaks. \n     The other listens. \n```\n\nComputercommunicatie vereist ook overeengekomen procedures. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"eaf8caac81a6b4ef721e5362cf483e39f879a92c8ae3e847ec8c3af50ec9eb0f","markdown":"## La communication nécessite des règles \n\nImaginez une conversation où chacun utilise une langue différente. \n\nLa communication serait difficile. \n\nLes ordinateurs sont confrontés au même défi. \n\nIls ont besoin de règles communes. \n\n### Protocoles \n\nUn protocole est un ensemble de règles qui définissent comment la communication se déroule. \n\nLes protocoles spécifient : \n\n- Le format des messages \n\n- Les méthodes de transmission \n\n- La gestion des erreurs \n\n- L'interprétation de l'information \n\n\n\n### Analogie du quotidien \n\nLa communication humaine repose sur des règles. \n\nPar exemple : \n\n```text\n     One person speaks. \n     The other listens. \n```\n\nLa communication informatique nécessite également des procédures convenues à l'avance. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"eaf8caac81a6b4ef721e5362cf483e39f879a92c8ae3e847ec8c3af50ec9eb0f","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Packets \n\nInformation sent across networks is divided into smaller pieces called packets. \n\n### Why Packets? \n\nImagine sending a large book. \n\nInstead of transporting the entire book as a single object, you divide it into pages. \n\nPackets work similarly. \n\n \n\n### Packet Contents \n\nA packet typically contains: \n\n```text\n     Source Address \n     Destination Address \n     Data \n     Control Information \n```\n\n### Benefits \n\nPackets: \n- Improve efficiency \n\n- Support sharing of network resources \n\n- Allow information to be retransmitted if lost ","output":"","result":"## Packets \n\nInformation sent across networks is divided into smaller pieces called packets. \n\n### Why Packets? \n\nImagine sending a large book. \n\nInstead of transporting the entire book as a single object, you divide it into pages. \n\nPackets work similarly. \n\n \n\n### Packet Contents \n\nA packet typically contains: \n\n```text\n     Source Address \n     Destination Address \n     Data \n     Control Information \n```\n\n### Benefits \n\nPackets: \n- Improve efficiency \n\n- Support sharing of network resources \n\n- Allow information to be retransmitted if lost ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3475-packets\">\n<h1>Packets</h1>\n<p>Information sent across networks is divided into smaller pieces called packets.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3475-why-packets\">\n<h1>Why Packets?</h1>\n<p>Imagine sending a large book.</p>\n<p>Instead of transporting the entire book as a single object, you divide it into pages.</p>\n<p>Packets work similarly.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3475-packet-contents\">\n<h1>Packet Contents</h1>\n<p>A packet typically contains:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Source Address \n     Destination Address \n     Data \n     Control Information </pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3475-benefits\">\n<h1>Benefits</h1>\n<p>Packets:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Improve efficiency</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Support sharing of network resources</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Allow information to be retransmitted if lost</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"8dfd40b58a446705d2c14714792411f2e318ecf860190421cd83b1c447c93d0e","markdown":"## Pakketten \n\nInformatie die over netwerken wordt verzonden, wordt opgedeeld in kleinere stukjes die pakketten worden genoemd. \n\n### Waarom pakketten? \n\nStel je voor dat je een groot boek verstuurt. \n\nIn plaats van het hele boek als één object te vervoeren, verdeel je het in pagina's. \n\nPakketten werken op een vergelijkbare manier. \n\n \n\n### Inhoud van een pakket \n\nEen pakket bevat doorgaans: \n\n```text\n     Source Address \n     Destination Address \n     Data \n     Control Information \n```\n\n### Voordelen \n\nPakketten: \n- Verbeteren de efficiëntie \n\n- Ondersteunen het delen van netwerkbronnen \n\n- Maken het mogelijk om informatie opnieuw te verzenden als deze verloren gaat"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"8dfd40b58a446705d2c14714792411f2e318ecf860190421cd83b1c447c93d0e","markdown":"## Paquets \n\nLes informations envoyées sur les réseaux sont divisées en petites unités appelées paquets. \n\n### Pourquoi des paquets ? \n\nImaginez que vous envoyiez un gros livre. \n\nAu lieu de transporter le livre entier comme un seul objet, vous le divisez en pages. \n\nLes paquets fonctionnent de manière similaire. \n\n \n\n### Contenu d'un paquet \n\nUn paquet contient généralement : \n\n```text\n     Source Address \n     Destination Address \n     Data \n     Control Information \n```\n\n### Avantages \n\nLes paquets : \n- Améliorent l'efficacité \n\n- Favorisent le partage des ressources réseau \n\n- Permettent de retransmettre les informations en cas de perte "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"8dfd40b58a446705d2c14714792411f2e318ecf860190421cd83b1c447c93d0e","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Addresses on the Internet \n\nFor communication to occur, devices need addresses. \n\n### Postal Analogy \n\nWhen sending a letter, you need: \n\n```text\n     Sender Address \n\n     Recipient Address \n```\n\nNetworks operate similarly. \n\n### IP Addresses \n\nEvery device connected to a network receives an IP address. \n\nIP stands for: \n\n```text\n     Internet Protocol \n```\n\n### Example \n\nAn IP address may look like: \n\n```text\n     192.168.1.10 \n```\n\nor \n\n```text\n     2001:db8::1 \n```\n\n### Purpose \n\nIP addresses identify devices and allow information to reach the correct destination. ","output":"","result":"## Addresses on the Internet \n\nFor communication to occur, devices need addresses. \n\n### Postal Analogy \n\nWhen sending a letter, you need: \n\n```text\n     Sender Address \n\n     Recipient Address \n```\n\nNetworks operate similarly. \n\n### IP Addresses \n\nEvery device connected to a network receives an IP address. \n\nIP stands for: \n\n```text\n     Internet Protocol \n```\n\n### Example \n\nAn IP address may look like: \n\n```text\n     192.168.1.10 \n```\n\nor \n\n```text\n     2001:db8::1 \n```\n\n### Purpose \n\nIP addresses identify devices and allow information to reach the correct destination. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3476-addresses-on-the-internet\">\n<h1>Addresses on the Internet</h1>\n<p>For communication to occur, devices need addresses.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3476-postal-analogy\">\n<h1>Postal Analogy</h1>\n<p>When sending a letter, you need:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Sender Address \n\n     Recipient Address </pre>\n<p>Networks operate similarly.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3476-ip-addresses\">\n<h1>IP Addresses</h1>\n<p>Every device connected to a network receives an IP address.</p>\n<p>IP stands for:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Internet Protocol </pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3476-example\">\n<h1>Example</h1>\n<p>An IP address may look like:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     192.168.1.10 </pre>\n<p>or</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     2001:db8::1 </pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3476-purpose\">\n<h1>Purpose</h1>\n<p>IP addresses identify devices and allow information to reach the correct destination.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"74c047e96c53ed39bac3b25818264fa621cef89d771b0174e9a746978a07fc83","markdown":"## Adressen op het internet \n\nOm communicatie mogelijk te maken, hebben apparaten adressen nodig. \n\n### Analogie met de post \n\nAls je een brief verstuurt, heb je nodig: \n\n```text\n     Sender Address \n\n     Recipient Address \n```\n\nNetwerken werken op een vergelijkbare manier. \n\n### IP-adressen \n\nElk apparaat dat met een netwerk is verbonden, krijgt een IP-adres. \n\nIP staat voor: \n\n```text\n     Internet Protocol \n```\n\n### Voorbeeld \n\nEen IP-adres kan er zo uitzien: \n\n```text\n     192.168.1.10 \n```\n\nof \n\n```text\n     2001:db8::1 \n```\n\n### Doel \n\nIP-adressen identificeren apparaten en zorgen ervoor dat informatie de juiste bestemming bereikt. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"74c047e96c53ed39bac3b25818264fa621cef89d771b0174e9a746978a07fc83","markdown":"## Adresses sur Internet \n\nPour que la communication ait lieu, les appareils ont besoin d'adresses. \n\n### Analogie postale \n\nLorsque vous envoyez une lettre, vous avez besoin de : \n\n```text\n     Sender Address \n\n     Recipient Address \n```\n\nLes réseaux fonctionnent de manière similaire. \n\n### Adresses IP \n\nChaque appareil connecté à un réseau reçoit une adresse IP. \n\nIP signifie : \n\n```text\n     Internet Protocol \n```\n\n### Exemple \n\nUne adresse IP peut ressembler à : \n\n```text\n     192.168.1.10 \n```\n\nou \n\n```text\n     2001:db8::1 \n```\n\n### Objectif \n\nLes adresses IP identifient les appareils et permettent aux informations d'atteindre la bonne destination. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"74c047e96c53ed39bac3b25818264fa621cef89d771b0174e9a746978a07fc83","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Domain Names \n\nHumans are poor at memorizing numerical addresses. \n\nImagine remembering: \n\n```text\n     142.250.184.206 \n```\ninstead of: \n\n```text\n     google.com \n```\n\n### Domain Names \n\nDomain names provide human-friendly names for computers and services. \n\nExamples: \n\n```text\n     google.com \n     microsoft.com \n     wikipedia.org \n```\n\n### Benefits \n\nDomain names are: \n\n- Easier to remember \n\n- Easier to communicate \n\n- Easier to organize ","output":"","result":"## Domain Names \n\nHumans are poor at memorizing numerical addresses. \n\nImagine remembering: \n\n```text\n     142.250.184.206 \n```\ninstead of: \n\n```text\n     google.com \n```\n\n### Domain Names \n\nDomain names provide human-friendly names for computers and services. \n\nExamples: \n\n```text\n     google.com \n     microsoft.com \n     wikipedia.org \n```\n\n### Benefits \n\nDomain names are: \n\n- Easier to remember \n\n- Easier to communicate \n\n- Easier to organize ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3477-domain-names\">\n<h1>Domain Names</h1>\n<p>Humans are poor at memorizing numerical addresses.</p>\n<p>Imagine remembering:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     142.250.184.206 </pre>\n<p>instead of:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     google.com </pre>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3477-domain-names-2\">\n<h1>Domain Names</h1>\n<p>Domain names provide human-friendly names for computers and services.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     google.com \n     microsoft.com \n     wikipedia.org </pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3477-benefits\">\n<h1>Benefits</h1>\n<p>Domain names are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Easier to remember</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Easier to communicate</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Easier to organize</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"17525c28c36625712f2c1315cda24b224a1a3eebb1855f731922999dac1902bb","markdown":"## Domeinnamen \n\nMensen zijn slecht in het onthouden van numerieke adressen. \n\nStel je voor dat je dit moet onthouden: \n\n```text\n     142.250.184.206 \n```\nin plaats van: \n\n```text\n     google.com \n```\n\n### Domeinnamen \n\nDomeinnamen bieden mensvriendelijke namen voor computers en diensten. \n\nVoorbeelden: \n\n```text\n     google.com \n     microsoft.com \n     wikipedia.org \n```\n\n### Voordelen \n\nDomeinnamen zijn: \n\n- Gemakkelijker te onthouden \n\n- Gemakkelijker te communiceren \n\n- Gemakkelijker te organiseren "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"17525c28c36625712f2c1315cda24b224a1a3eebb1855f731922999dac1902bb","markdown":"## Noms de domaine \n\nLes humains sont peu doués pour mémoriser des adresses numériques. \n\nImaginez devoir vous souvenir de : \n\n```text\n     142.250.184.206 \n```\nau lieu de : \n\n```text\n     google.com \n```\n\n### Noms de domaine \n\nLes noms de domaine fournissent des noms conviviaux pour les ordinateurs et les services. \n\nExemples : \n\n```text\n     google.com \n     microsoft.com \n     wikipedia.org \n```\n\n### Avantages \n\nLes noms de domaine sont : \n\n- Plus faciles à mémoriser \n\n- Plus faciles à communiquer \n\n- Plus faciles à organiser "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"17525c28c36625712f2c1315cda24b224a1a3eebb1855f731922999dac1902bb","language":"English"}},{"input":"### DNS: The Internet's Phone Book \n\nDNS stands for: \n\n```text\n     Domain Name System \n```\n\nIts purpose is to translate domain names into IP addresses. \n\n### Example \n\nUser enters: \n\n```text\n     www.example.com \n```\n\nDNS returns: \n```text\n     93.184.216.34 \n```\n\nThe browser can then contact the correct server. \n\n### Analogy \n\nDNS is similar to a contact list on a phone. \n\nYou remember: \n\n```text\n     Ben \n```\n\nrather than: \n\n```text\n     +32 xxx xx xx xx \n```\n\nDNS performs the same function for computers. ","output":"","result":"### DNS: The Internet's Phone Book \n\nDNS stands for: \n\n```text\n     Domain Name System \n```\n\nIts purpose is to translate domain names into IP addresses. \n\n### Example \n\nUser enters: \n\n```text\n     www.example.com \n```\n\nDNS returns: \n```text\n     93.184.216.34 \n```\n\nThe browser can then contact the correct server. \n\n### Analogy \n\nDNS is similar to a contact list on a phone. \n\nYou remember: \n\n```text\n     Ben \n```\n\nrather than: \n\n```text\n     +32 xxx xx xx xx \n```\n\nDNS performs the same function for computers. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3478-dns-the-internets-phone-book\">\n<h1>DNS: The Internet’s Phone Book</h1>\n<p>DNS stands for:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Domain Name System </pre>\n<p>Its purpose is to translate domain names into IP addresses.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3478-example\">\n<h1>Example</h1>\n<p>User enters:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     www.example.com </pre>\n<p>DNS returns:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     93.184.216.34 </pre>\n<p>The browser can then contact the correct server.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3478-analogy\">\n<h1>Analogy</h1>\n<p>DNS is similar to a contact list on a phone.</p>\n<p>You remember:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Ben </pre>\n<p>rather than:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     +32 xxx xx xx xx </pre>\n<p>DNS performs the same function for computers.</p>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"08bb5f56bb5732d4418849c28c42ae650b624d5373d346de12cbec61c4bc0680","markdown":"### DNS: Het Telefoonboek van het Internet \n\nDNS staat voor: \n\n```text\n     Domain Name System \n```\n\nHet doel ervan is om domeinnamen te vertalen naar IP-adressen. \n\n### Voorbeeld \n\nGebruiker voert in: \n\n```text\n     www.example.com \n```\n\nDNS geeft terug: \n```text\n     93.184.216.34 \n```\n\nDe browser kan dan contact opnemen met de juiste server. \n\n### Analogie \n\nDNS lijkt op een contactenlijst op een telefoon. \n\nJe onthoudt: \n\n```text\n     Ben \n```\n\nin plaats van: \n\n```text\n     +32 xxx xx xx xx \n```\n\nDNS vervult dezelfde functie voor computers. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"08bb5f56bb5732d4418849c28c42ae650b624d5373d346de12cbec61c4bc0680","markdown":"### DNS : L'annuaire téléphonique d'Internet \n\nDNS signifie : \n\n```text\n     Domain Name System \n```\n\nSon objectif est de traduire les noms de domaine en adresses IP. \n\n### Exemple \n\nL'utilisateur saisit : \n\n```text\n     www.example.com \n```\n\nLe DNS renvoie : \n```text\n     93.184.216.34 \n```\n\nLe navigateur peut alors contacter le bon serveur. \n\n### Analogie \n\nLe DNS est semblable à une liste de contacts sur un téléphone. \n\nVous vous souvenez de : \n\n```text\n     Ben \n```\n\nplutôt que de : \n\n```text\n     +32 xxx xx xx xx \n```\n\nLe DNS remplit la même fonction pour les ordinateurs. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"08bb5f56bb5732d4418849c28c42ae650b624d5373d346de12cbec61c4bc0680","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Clients and Servers \n\nMost Internet services follow a client-server model. \n\n### Client \n\nA client requests a service. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Web browser \n\n- Mobile app \n\n- Email application \n\n### Server \n\nA server provides a service. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Website server \n\n- Email server \n\n- Video streaming server \n\n### Example \n\n```text\n      Browser \n      (Client) \nRequest ↓  ↑ Response\n      Website \n      (Server) \n```\n\n### Everyday Analogy \n\nRestaurant: \n\n```text\n     Customer = Client \n     Kitchen = Server \n```\n\nThe customer requests a service. \n\nThe kitchen provides it. ","output":"","result":"## Clients and Servers \n\nMost Internet services follow a client-server model. \n\n### Client \n\nA client requests a service. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Web browser \n\n- Mobile app \n\n- Email application \n\n### Server \n\nA server provides a service. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Website server \n\n- Email server \n\n- Video streaming server \n\n### Example \n\n```text\n      Browser \n      (Client) \nRequest ↓  ↑ Response\n      Website \n      (Server) \n```\n\n### Everyday Analogy \n\nRestaurant: \n\n```text\n     Customer = Client \n     Kitchen = Server \n```\n\nThe customer requests a service. \n\nThe kitchen provides it. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3479-clients-and-servers\">\n<h1>Clients and Servers</h1>\n<p>Most Internet services follow a client-server model.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3479-client\">\n<h1>Client</h1>\n<p>A client requests a service.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Web browser</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Mobile app</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Email application</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3479-server\">\n<h1>Server</h1>\n<p>A server provides a service.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Website server</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Email server</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Video streaming server</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3479-example\">\n<h1>Example</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">      Browser \n      (Client) \nRequest ↓  ↑ Response\n      Website \n      (Server) </pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3479-everyday-analogy\">\n<h1>Everyday Analogy</h1>\n<p>Restaurant:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Customer = Client \n     Kitchen = Server </pre>\n<p>The customer requests a service.</p>\n<p>The kitchen provides it.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"36f846f8749a03c6b1f21f7ae7dc2fedf5b737a9ffd522182456e4373a0888d9","markdown":"## Clients en Servers\n\nDe meeste internetdiensten volgen een client-servermodel.\n\n### Client\n\nEen client vraagt een dienst aan.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Webbrowser\n\n- Mobiele app\n\n- E-mailtoepassing\n\n### Server\n\nEen server levert een dienst.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Websiteserver\n\n- E-mailserver\n\n- Videostreamingserver\n\n### Voorbeeld\n\n```text\n      Browser \n      (Client) \nRequest ↓  ↑ Response\n      Website \n      (Server) \n```\n\n### Alledaagse Analogie\n\nRestaurant:\n\n```text\n     Customer = Client \n     Kitchen = Server \n```\n\nDe klant vraagt een dienst aan.\n\nDe keuken levert deze."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"36f846f8749a03c6b1f21f7ae7dc2fedf5b737a9ffd522182456e4373a0888d9","markdown":"## Clients et serveurs \n\nLa plupart des services Internet suivent un modèle client-serveur. \n\n### Client \n\nUn client demande un service. \n\nExemples : \n\n- Navigateur web \n\n- Application mobile \n\n- Application de messagerie \n\n### Serveur \n\nUn serveur fournit un service. \n\nExemples : \n\n- Serveur de site web \n\n- Serveur de messagerie \n\n- Serveur de streaming vidéo \n\n### Exemple \n\n```text\n      Browser \n      (Client) \nRequest ↓  ↑ Response\n      Website \n      (Server) \n```\n\n### Analogie du quotidien \n\nRestaurant : \n\n```text\n     Customer = Client \n     Kitchen = Server \n```\n\nLe client demande un service. \n\nLa cuisine le fournit. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"36f846f8749a03c6b1f21f7ae7dc2fedf5b737a9ffd522182456e4373a0888d9","language":"English"}},{"input":"## The Internet Protocol (IP) \n\nThe Internet Protocol is responsible for delivering packets between devices. \n\n \n\n### Responsibilities \n\nIP determines: \n\n- Source address \n\n- Destination address \n\n- Routing through networks \n\n \n\n### Important Observation \n\nIP attempts delivery. \n\nIt does not guarantee delivery. \n\nFor reliability, additional protocols are needed. ","output":"","result":"## The Internet Protocol (IP) \n\nThe Internet Protocol is responsible for delivering packets between devices. \n\n \n\n### Responsibilities \n\nIP determines: \n\n- Source address \n\n- Destination address \n\n- Routing through networks \n\n \n\n### Important Observation \n\nIP attempts delivery. \n\nIt does not guarantee delivery. \n\nFor reliability, additional protocols are needed. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3480-the-internet-protocol-ip\">\n<h1>The Internet Protocol (IP)</h1>\n<p>The Internet Protocol is responsible for delivering packets between devices.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3480-responsibilities\">\n<h1>Responsibilities</h1>\n<p>IP determines:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Source address</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Destination address</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Routing through networks</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3480-important-observation\">\n<h1>Important Observation</h1>\n<p>IP attempts delivery.</p>\n<p>It does not guarantee delivery.</p>\n<p>For reliability, additional protocols are needed.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"a2cc2eb02c817c9b57ef8f053ea5d936ddc2aca234ba1fc5a347257aaefee719","markdown":"## Het Internet Protocol (IP) \n\nHet Internet Protocol is verantwoordelijk voor het afleveren van pakketten tussen apparaten. \n\n \n\n### Verantwoordelijkheden \n\nIP bepaalt: \n\n- Bronadres \n\n- Bestemmingsadres \n\n- Routering door netwerken \n\n \n\n### Belangrijke observatie \n\nIP probeert af te leveren. \n\nHet garandeert geen aflevering. \n\nVoor betrouwbaarheid zijn aanvullende protocollen nodig. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"a2cc2eb02c817c9b57ef8f053ea5d936ddc2aca234ba1fc5a347257aaefee719","markdown":"## Le protocole Internet (IP) \n\nLe protocole Internet est responsable de l'acheminement des paquets entre les appareils. \n\n \n\n### Responsabilités \n\nIP détermine : \n\n- L'adresse source \n\n- L'adresse de destination \n\n- Le routage à travers les réseaux \n\n \n\n### Observation importante \n\nIP tente la livraison. \n\nIl ne garantit pas la livraison. \n\nPour assurer la fiabilité, des protocoles supplémentaires sont nécessaires. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"a2cc2eb02c817c9b57ef8f053ea5d936ddc2aca234ba1fc5a347257aaefee719","language":"English"}},{"input":"## TCP \n\nTCP stands for: \n\n```text\n     Transmission Control Protocol \n```\n\nTCP provides reliable communication. \n\n### Responsibilities \n\nTCP ensures: \n\n- Packets arrive \n\n- Packets arrive correctly \n\n- Packets are reassembled in proper order \n\n### Analogy \n\nImagine sending numbered pages. \n\nTCP checks: \n\n```text\n     Page 5 arrived \n\n     Page 6 arrived \n\n     Page 7 arrived \n```\n\nIf page 6 is missing, TCP requests it again. \n\n\n### Applications \n\nTCP is commonly used for: \n\n- Websites \n\n- Email \n\n- File transfers \n\nwhere reliability is important. ","output":"","result":"## TCP \n\nTCP stands for: \n\n```text\n     Transmission Control Protocol \n```\n\nTCP provides reliable communication. \n\n### Responsibilities \n\nTCP ensures: \n\n- Packets arrive \n\n- Packets arrive correctly \n\n- Packets are reassembled in proper order \n\n### Analogy \n\nImagine sending numbered pages. \n\nTCP checks: \n\n```text\n     Page 5 arrived \n\n     Page 6 arrived \n\n     Page 7 arrived \n```\n\nIf page 6 is missing, TCP requests it again. \n\n\n### Applications \n\nTCP is commonly used for: \n\n- Websites \n\n- Email \n\n- File transfers \n\nwhere reliability is important. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3481-tcp\">\n<h1>TCP</h1>\n<p>TCP stands for:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Transmission Control Protocol </pre>\n<p>TCP provides reliable communication.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3481-responsibilities\">\n<h1>Responsibilities</h1>\n<p>TCP ensures:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Packets arrive</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Packets arrive correctly</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Packets are reassembled in proper order</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3481-analogy\">\n<h1>Analogy</h1>\n<p>Imagine sending numbered pages.</p>\n<p>TCP checks:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Page 5 arrived \n\n     Page 6 arrived \n\n     Page 7 arrived </pre>\n<p>If page 6 is missing, TCP requests it again.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3481-applications\">\n<h1>Applications</h1>\n<p>TCP is commonly used for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Websites</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Email</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>File transfers</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>where reliability is important.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"364c6de469d6ab0b82748fd4c2ce63c66d3bde0aa39ef32f28b3e72a58211655","markdown":"## TCP \n\nTCP staat voor: \n\n```text\n     Transmission Control Protocol \n```\n\nTCP zorgt voor betrouwbare communicatie. \n\n### Verantwoordelijkheden \n\nTCP zorgt ervoor dat: \n\n- Pakketten aankomen \n\n- Pakketten correct aankomen \n\n- Pakketten in de juiste volgorde worden samengevoegd \n\n### Analogie \n\nStel je voor dat je genummerde pagina's verstuurt. \n\nTCP controleert: \n\n```text\n     Page 5 arrived \n\n     Page 6 arrived \n\n     Page 7 arrived \n```\n\nAls pagina 6 ontbreekt, vraagt TCP deze opnieuw aan. \n\n\n### Toepassingen \n\nTCP wordt vaak gebruikt voor: \n\n- Websites \n\n- E-mail \n\n- Bestandsoverdrachten \n\nwaar betrouwbaarheid belangrijk is. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"364c6de469d6ab0b82748fd4c2ce63c66d3bde0aa39ef32f28b3e72a58211655","markdown":"## TCP \n\nTCP signifie : \n\n```text\n     Transmission Control Protocol \n```\n\nTCP assure une communication fiable. \n\n### Responsabilités \n\nTCP garantit que : \n\n- Les paquets arrivent \n\n- Les paquets arrivent correctement \n\n- Les paquets sont réassemblés dans le bon ordre \n\n### Analogie \n\nImaginez l'envoi de pages numérotées. \n\nTCP vérifie : \n\n```text\n     Page 5 arrived \n\n     Page 6 arrived \n\n     Page 7 arrived \n```\n\nSi la page 6 est manquante, TCP la redemande. \n\n\n### Applications \n\nTCP est couramment utilisé pour : \n\n- Les sites web \n\n- Les e-mails \n\n- Les transferts de fichiers \n\noù la fiabilité est importante. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"364c6de469d6ab0b82748fd4c2ce63c66d3bde0aa39ef32f28b3e72a58211655","language":"English"}},{"input":"## UDP \n\nUDP stands for: \n\n```text\n     User Datagram Protocol \n```\n\nUDP is simpler than TCP. \n\n\n### Characteristics \n\nUDP: \n\n- Is faster \n\n- Uses less overhead \n\n- Does not guarantee delivery \n\n \n\n### Analogy \n\nUDP is like a live conversation. \n\nIf one word is missed: \n\n```text\n     Conversation continues \n```\n\nThe missing word is usually not requested again. \n\n \n\n### Applications \n\nUDP is often used for: \n\n- Video conferencing \n\n- Online gaming \n\n- Streaming \n\nwhere speed is more important than perfect reliability. ","output":"","result":"## UDP \n\nUDP stands for: \n\n```text\n     User Datagram Protocol \n```\n\nUDP is simpler than TCP. \n\n\n### Characteristics \n\nUDP: \n\n- Is faster \n\n- Uses less overhead \n\n- Does not guarantee delivery \n\n \n\n### Analogy \n\nUDP is like a live conversation. \n\nIf one word is missed: \n\n```text\n     Conversation continues \n```\n\nThe missing word is usually not requested again. \n\n \n\n### Applications \n\nUDP is often used for: \n\n- Video conferencing \n\n- Online gaming \n\n- Streaming \n\nwhere speed is more important than perfect reliability. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3482-udp\">\n<h1>UDP</h1>\n<p>UDP stands for:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     User Datagram Protocol </pre>\n<p>UDP is simpler than TCP.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3482-characteristics\">\n<h1>Characteristics</h1>\n<p>UDP:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Is faster</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Uses less overhead</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Does not guarantee delivery</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3482-analogy\">\n<h1>Analogy</h1>\n<p>UDP is like a live conversation.</p>\n<p>If one word is missed:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Conversation continues </pre>\n<p>The missing word is usually not requested again.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3482-applications\">\n<h1>Applications</h1>\n<p>UDP is often used for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Video conferencing</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Online gaming</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Streaming</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>where speed is more important than perfect reliability.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"95dc67b94c0f4345d2bedfab0196a4331e2f7bbf371128e4127cba0830540edd","markdown":"## UDP \n\nUDP staat voor: \n\n```text\n     User Datagram Protocol \n```\n\nUDP is eenvoudiger dan TCP. \n\n\n### Kenmerken \n\nUDP: \n\n- Is sneller \n\n- Gebruikt minder overhead \n\n- Garandeert geen aflevering \n\n \n\n### Analogie \n\nUDP is als een live gesprek. \n\nAls één woord wordt gemist: \n\n```text\n     Conversation continues \n```\n\nHet gemiste woord wordt meestal niet opnieuw opgevraagd. \n\n \n\n### Toepassingen \n\nUDP wordt vaak gebruikt voor: \n\n- Videoconferentie \n\n- Online gamen \n\n- Streaming \n\nwaar snelheid belangrijker is dan perfecte betrouwbaarheid. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"95dc67b94c0f4345d2bedfab0196a4331e2f7bbf371128e4127cba0830540edd","markdown":"## UDP \n\nUDP signifie : \n\n```text\n     User Datagram Protocol \n```\n\nUDP est plus simple que TCP. \n\n\n### Caractéristiques \n\nUDP : \n\n- Est plus rapide \n\n- Utilise moins de surcharge \n\n- Ne garantit pas la livraison \n\n \n\n### Analogie \n\nUDP est comme une conversation en direct. \n\nSi un mot est manqué : \n\n```text\n     Conversation continues \n```\n\nLe mot manquant n'est généralement pas redemandé. \n\n \n\n### Applications \n\nUDP est souvent utilisé pour : \n\n- La visioconférence \n\n- Les jeux en ligne \n\n- Le streaming \n\noù la vitesse est plus importante qu'une fiabilité parfaite. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"95dc67b94c0f4345d2bedfab0196a4331e2f7bbf371128e4127cba0830540edd","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Routing \n\nPackets may travel through many networks before reaching their destination. \n\n \n\n### Routers \n\nRouters are devices that forward packets from one network to another. \n\n \n\n### Example \n\n```text\n     Computer \n        ↓ \n     Home Router \n        ↓ \n     Internet Provider \n        ↓ \n     Several Routers \n        ↓ \n     Destination Server \n```\n\n### Analogy \n\nRouting is similar to road navigation. \n\nRoad signs guide vehicles. \n\nRouters guide packets. ","output":"","result":"## Routing \n\nPackets may travel through many networks before reaching their destination. \n\n \n\n### Routers \n\nRouters are devices that forward packets from one network to another. \n\n \n\n### Example \n\n```text\n     Computer \n        ↓ \n     Home Router \n        ↓ \n     Internet Provider \n        ↓ \n     Several Routers \n        ↓ \n     Destination Server \n```\n\n### Analogy \n\nRouting is similar to road navigation. \n\nRoad signs guide vehicles. \n\nRouters guide packets. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3483-routing\">\n<h1>Routing</h1>\n<p>Packets may travel through many networks before reaching their destination.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3483-routers\">\n<h1>Routers</h1>\n<p>Routers are devices that forward packets from one network to another.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3483-example\">\n<h1>Example</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Computer \n        ↓ \n     Home Router \n        ↓ \n     Internet Provider \n        ↓ \n     Several Routers \n        ↓ \n     Destination Server </pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3483-analogy\">\n<h1>Analogy</h1>\n<p>Routing is similar to road navigation.</p>\n<p>Road signs guide vehicles.</p>\n<p>Routers guide packets.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"eb7eab763ba7d9b64c9d1d0886c0006a398868da729cec1436d11d430cfa4002","markdown":"## Routering \n\nPakketten kunnen door veel netwerken reizen voordat ze hun bestemming bereiken. \n\n \n\n### Routers \n\nRouters zijn apparaten die pakketten van het ene netwerk naar het andere doorsturen. \n\n \n\n### Voorbeeld \n\n```text\n     Computer \n        ↓ \n     Home Router \n        ↓ \n     Internet Provider \n        ↓ \n     Several Routers \n        ↓ \n     Destination Server \n```\n\n### Analogie \n\nRoutering lijkt op wegnavigatie. \n\nVerkeersborden begeleiden voertuigen. \n\nRouters begeleiden pakketten. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"eb7eab763ba7d9b64c9d1d0886c0006a398868da729cec1436d11d430cfa4002","markdown":"## Routage \n\nLes paquets peuvent traverser de nombreux réseaux avant d'atteindre leur destination. \n\n \n\n### Routeurs \n\nLes routeurs sont des dispositifs qui transmettent les paquets d'un réseau à un autre. \n\n \n\n### Exemple \n\n```text\n     Computer \n        ↓ \n     Home Router \n        ↓ \n     Internet Provider \n        ↓ \n     Several Routers \n        ↓ \n     Destination Server \n```\n\n### Analogie \n\nLe routage est similaire à la navigation routière. \n\nLes panneaux de signalisation guident les véhicules. \n\nLes routeurs guident les paquets. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"eb7eab763ba7d9b64c9d1d0886c0006a398868da729cec1436d11d430cfa4002","language":"English"}},{"input":"## The World Wide Web \n\nMany people confuse: \n\n```text\n     Internet \n```\n\nand \n```text\n     Web \n```\n\nThey are not the same thing. \n\n\n### Internet \n\nThe infrastructure. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Networks \n\n- Routers \n\n- Protocols \n\n### World Wide Web \n\nA service running on top of the Internet. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Websites \n\n- Web applications \n\n\n### Important Observation \n\nThe Web is part of the Internet. \n\nThe Internet is larger than the Web. ","output":"","result":"## The World Wide Web \n\nMany people confuse: \n\n```text\n     Internet \n```\n\nand \n```text\n     Web \n```\n\nThey are not the same thing. \n\n\n### Internet \n\nThe infrastructure. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Networks \n\n- Routers \n\n- Protocols \n\n### World Wide Web \n\nA service running on top of the Internet. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Websites \n\n- Web applications \n\n\n### Important Observation \n\nThe Web is part of the Internet. \n\nThe Internet is larger than the Web. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3484-the-world-wide-web\">\n<h1>The World Wide Web</h1>\n<p>Many people confuse:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Internet </pre>\n<p>and</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Web </pre>\n<p>They are not the same thing.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3484-internet\">\n<h1>Internet</h1>\n<p>The infrastructure.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Networks</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Routers</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Protocols</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3484-world-wide-web\">\n<h1>World Wide Web</h1>\n<p>A service running on top of the Internet.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Websites</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Web applications</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3484-important-observation\">\n<h1>Important Observation</h1>\n<p>The Web is part of the Internet.</p>\n<p>The Internet is larger than the Web.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"69f6c30eb284374b67e67e6136ecf1cb9ac457ae5dfd06ab98b3e0cce5861efc","markdown":"## Het World Wide Web\n\nVeel mensen verwarren:\n\n```text\n     Internet \n```\n\nen\n```text\n     Web \n```\n\nHet zijn niet dezelfde dingen.\n\n\n### Internet\n\nDe infrastructuur.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Netwerken\n\n- Routers\n\n- Protocollen\n\n### World Wide Web\n\nEen dienst die bovenop het internet draait.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Websites\n\n- Webapplicaties\n\n\n### Belangrijke opmerking\n\nHet Web maakt deel uit van het internet.\n\nHet internet is groter dan het Web."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"69f6c30eb284374b67e67e6136ecf1cb9ac457ae5dfd06ab98b3e0cce5861efc","markdown":"## Le World Wide Web \n\nBeaucoup de gens confondent : \n\n```text\n     Internet \n```\n\net \n```text\n     Web \n```\n\nCe ne sont pas la même chose. \n\n\n### Internet \n\nL'infrastructure. \n\nExemples : \n\n- Réseaux \n\n- Routeurs \n\n- Protocoles \n\n### World Wide Web \n\nUn service fonctionnant au-dessus d'Internet. \n\nExemples : \n\n- Sites web \n\n- Applications web \n\n\n### Observation importante \n\nLe Web fait partie d'Internet. \n\nInternet est plus vaste que le Web. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"69f6c30eb284374b67e67e6136ecf1cb9ac457ae5dfd06ab98b3e0cce5861efc","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Web Browsers \n\nA browser enables users to access web content. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Chrome \n\n- Edge \n\n- Firefox \n\n- Safari \n\n \n\n### Browser Responsibilities \n\nThe browser: \n\n- Requests web pages \n\n- Receives information \n\n- Displays content \n\n \n\n### Examples of Content \n\n- Text \n\n- Images \n\n- Videos \n\n- Interactive applications","output":"","result":"## Web Browsers \n\nA browser enables users to access web content. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Chrome \n\n- Edge \n\n- Firefox \n\n- Safari \n\n \n\n### Browser Responsibilities \n\nThe browser: \n\n- Requests web pages \n\n- Receives information \n\n- Displays content \n\n \n\n### Examples of Content \n\n- Text \n\n- Images \n\n- Videos \n\n- Interactive applications","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3485-web-browsers\">\n<h1>Web Browsers</h1>\n<p>A browser enables users to access web content.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Chrome</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Edge</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Firefox</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Safari</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3485-browser-responsibilities\">\n<h1>Browser Responsibilities</h1>\n<p>The browser:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Requests web pages</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Receives information</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Displays content</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3485-examples-of-content\">\n<h1>Examples of Content</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Text</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Images</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Videos</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Interactive applications</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"89594f78f1634b6a14d897309c599c79e2a579bbd5f08fa126da656d28524666","markdown":"## Webbrowsers \n\nEen browser stelt gebruikers in staat om toegang te krijgen tot webinhoud. \n\nVoorbeelden: \n\n- Chrome \n\n- Edge \n\n- Firefox \n\n- Safari \n\n \n\n### Verantwoordelijkheden van de browser \n\nDe browser: \n\n- Vraagt webpagina's op \n\n- Ontvangt informatie \n\n- Toont inhoud \n\n \n\n### Voorbeelden van inhoud \n\n- Tekst \n\n- Afbeeldingen \n\n- Video's \n\n- Interactieve applicaties"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"89594f78f1634b6a14d897309c599c79e2a579bbd5f08fa126da656d28524666","markdown":"## Navigateurs Web \n\nUn navigateur permet aux utilisateurs d'accéder au contenu web. \n\nExemples : \n\n- Chrome \n\n- Edge \n\n- Firefox \n\n- Safari \n\n \n\n### Responsabilités du navigateur \n\nLe navigateur : \n\n- Demande des pages web \n\n- Reçoit des informations \n\n- Affiche le contenu \n\n \n\n### Exemples de contenu \n\n- Texte \n\n- Images \n\n- Vidéos \n\n- Applications interactives"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"89594f78f1634b6a14d897309c599c79e2a579bbd5f08fa126da656d28524666","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Web Servers \n\nA web server stores and provides web content. \n\n \n\n### Example \n\nWhen visiting: \n\n```text\n     www.university.edu \n```\n\nthe browser contacts a web server that provides: \n\n- Text \n\n- Images \n\n- Layout information \n\n \n\n### Response \n\nThe browser receives the information and displays the page. ","output":"","result":"## Web Servers \n\nA web server stores and provides web content. \n\n \n\n### Example \n\nWhen visiting: \n\n```text\n     www.university.edu \n```\n\nthe browser contacts a web server that provides: \n\n- Text \n\n- Images \n\n- Layout information \n\n \n\n### Response \n\nThe browser receives the information and displays the page. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3486-web-servers\">\n<h1>Web Servers</h1>\n<p>A web server stores and provides web content.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3486-example\">\n<h1>Example</h1>\n<p>When visiting:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     www.university.edu </pre>\n<p>the browser contacts a web server that provides:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Text</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Images</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Layout information</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3486-response\">\n<h1>Response</h1>\n<p>The browser receives the information and displays the page.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"9b3731c0fbeff7405283129f35ffe603dc4021482747f46f8e7578d0595b23c1","markdown":"## Webservers \n\nEen webserver slaat webinhoud op en levert deze. \n\n \n\n### Voorbeeld \n\nBij het bezoeken van: \n\n```text\n     www.university.edu \n```\n\nneemt de browser contact op met een webserver die het volgende levert: \n\n- Tekst \n\n- Afbeeldingen \n\n- Opmaakinformatie \n\n \n\n### Antwoord \n\nDe browser ontvangt de informatie en toont de pagina. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"9b3731c0fbeff7405283129f35ffe603dc4021482747f46f8e7578d0595b23c1","markdown":"## Serveurs web \n\nUn serveur web stocke et fournit du contenu web. \n\n \n\n### Exemple \n\nLors de la visite de : \n\n```text\n     www.university.edu \n```\n\nle navigateur contacte un serveur web qui fournit : \n\n- Du texte \n\n- Des images \n\n- Des informations de mise en page \n\n \n\n### Réponse \n\nLe navigateur reçoit les informations et affiche la page. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"9b3731c0fbeff7405283129f35ffe603dc4021482747f46f8e7578d0595b23c1","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Cloud Computing \n\nMany modern services no longer run entirely on local computers. \n\nInstead they operate in the cloud. \n\n \n\n### What Is the Cloud? \n\nThe cloud simply refers to remote computers that provide services over a network. \n\n \n\nExamples \n\n- OneDrive \n\n- Google Drive \n\n- Netflix \n\n- Microsoft 365 \n\n- Online AI systems \n\n \n\n### Benefits \n\nCloud services provide: \n\n- Accessibility \n\n- Scalability \n\n- Resource sharing \n\n- Centralized management \n\n \n\n### Everyday Example \n\nInstead of storing a file locally: \n\n```text\n     Laptop \n```\n\nyou store it on: \n\n```text\n     Remote Server \n```\n\nand access it from anywhere. ","output":"","result":"## Cloud Computing \n\nMany modern services no longer run entirely on local computers. \n\nInstead they operate in the cloud. \n\n \n\n### What Is the Cloud? \n\nThe cloud simply refers to remote computers that provide services over a network. \n\n \n\nExamples \n\n- OneDrive \n\n- Google Drive \n\n- Netflix \n\n- Microsoft 365 \n\n- Online AI systems \n\n \n\n### Benefits \n\nCloud services provide: \n\n- Accessibility \n\n- Scalability \n\n- Resource sharing \n\n- Centralized management \n\n \n\n### Everyday Example \n\nInstead of storing a file locally: \n\n```text\n     Laptop \n```\n\nyou store it on: \n\n```text\n     Remote Server \n```\n\nand access it from anywhere. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3487-cloud-computing\">\n<h1>Cloud Computing</h1>\n<p>Many modern services no longer run entirely on local computers.</p>\n<p>Instead they operate in the cloud.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3487-what-is-the-cloud\">\n<h1>What Is the Cloud?</h1>\n<p>The cloud simply refers to remote computers that provide services over a network.</p>\n<p>Examples</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>OneDrive</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Google Drive</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Netflix</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Microsoft 365</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Online AI systems</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3487-benefits\">\n<h1>Benefits</h1>\n<p>Cloud services provide:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Accessibility</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Scalability</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Resource sharing</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Centralized management</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3487-everyday-example\">\n<h1>Everyday Example</h1>\n<p>Instead of storing a file locally:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Laptop </pre>\n<p>you store it on:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Remote Server </pre>\n<p>and access it from anywhere.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"9448feec007419694ad7d9f6a7624b1880f104d9ecbf6e86e8233098f7e543e0","markdown":"## Cloud Computing \n\nVeel moderne diensten draaien niet langer volledig op lokale computers. \n\nIn plaats daarvan werken ze in de cloud. \n\n \n\n### Wat Is de Cloud? \n\nDe cloud verwijst eenvoudigweg naar externe computers die diensten via een netwerk aanbieden. \n\n \n\nVoorbeelden \n\n- OneDrive \n\n- Google Drive \n\n- Netflix \n\n- Microsoft 365 \n\n- Online AI-systemen \n\n \n\n### Voordelen \n\nClouddiensten bieden: \n\n- Toegankelijkheid \n\n- Schaalbaarheid \n\n- Gedeeld gebruik van bronnen \n\n- Gecentraliseerd beheer \n\n \n\n### Alledaags Voorbeeld \n\nIn plaats van een bestand lokaal op te slaan: \n\n```text\n     Laptop \n```\n\nsla je het op in: \n\n```text\n     Remote Server \n```\n\nen heb je er overal toegang toe. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"9448feec007419694ad7d9f6a7624b1880f104d9ecbf6e86e8233098f7e543e0","markdown":"## Informatique en nuage \n\nDe nombreux services modernes ne fonctionnent plus entièrement sur des ordinateurs locaux. \n\nIls fonctionnent plutôt dans le cloud. \n\n \n\n### Qu'est-ce que le cloud ? \n\nLe cloud désigne simplement des ordinateurs distants qui fournissent des services via un réseau. \n\n \n\nExemples \n\n- OneDrive \n\n- Google Drive \n\n- Netflix \n\n- Microsoft 365 \n\n- Systèmes d'IA en ligne \n\n \n\n### Avantages \n\nLes services cloud offrent : \n\n- Accessibilité \n\n- Évolutivité \n\n- Partage des ressources \n\n- Gestion centralisée \n\n \n\n### Exemple du quotidien \n\nAu lieu de stocker un fichier localement : \n\n```text\n     Laptop \n```\n\nvous le stockez sur : \n\n```text\n     Remote Server \n```\n\net y accédez depuis n'importe où. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"9448feec007419694ad7d9f6a7624b1880f104d9ecbf6e86e8233098f7e543e0","language":"English"}},{"input":"## A Journey Through the Internet \n\nLet's follow what happens when a student visits: \n\n```text\n     www.example.com \n```\n\n### Step 1: User Enters Address \n\nThe student types: \n\n```text\n     www.example.com \n```\n\ninto a browser. \n\n \n\n### Step 2: DNS Lookup \n\nDNS translates: \n\n```text\n     www.example.com \n```\n\ninto an IP address. \n\n \n\n### Step 3: Contact the Server \n\nThe browser sends a request. \n\n```text\n     Client → Server \n```\n\n### Step 4: Routing \n\nPackets travel through multiple routers. \n\n```text\n     Home Network \n     ↓ \n     Internet Provider \n     ↓ \n     Internet \n     ↓ \n     Web Server \n```\n\n### Step 5: Server Response \n\nThe web server sends: \n\n- HTML \n\n- Images \n\n- Scripts \n\nback to the browser. \n\n### Step 6: Browser Displays the Page \n\nThe browser interprets the information and displays the website. \n\n \n\n### Remark \n\nThis entire process often completes in less than a second. ","output":"","result":"## A Journey Through the Internet \n\nLet's follow what happens when a student visits: \n\n```text\n     www.example.com \n```\n\n### Step 1: User Enters Address \n\nThe student types: \n\n```text\n     www.example.com \n```\n\ninto a browser. \n\n \n\n### Step 2: DNS Lookup \n\nDNS translates: \n\n```text\n     www.example.com \n```\n\ninto an IP address. \n\n \n\n### Step 3: Contact the Server \n\nThe browser sends a request. \n\n```text\n     Client → Server \n```\n\n### Step 4: Routing \n\nPackets travel through multiple routers. \n\n```text\n     Home Network \n     ↓ \n     Internet Provider \n     ↓ \n     Internet \n     ↓ \n     Web Server \n```\n\n### Step 5: Server Response \n\nThe web server sends: \n\n- HTML \n\n- Images \n\n- Scripts \n\nback to the browser. \n\n### Step 6: Browser Displays the Page \n\nThe browser interprets the information and displays the website. \n\n \n\n### Remark \n\nThis entire process often completes in less than a second. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3488-a-journey-through-the-internet\">\n<h1>A Journey Through the Internet</h1>\n<p>Let’s follow what happens when a student visits:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     www.example.com </pre>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3488-step-1-user-enters-address\">\n<h1>Step 1: User Enters Address</h1>\n<p>The student types:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     www.example.com </pre>\n<p>into a browser.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3488-step-2-dns-lookup\">\n<h1>Step 2: DNS Lookup</h1>\n<p>DNS translates:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     www.example.com </pre>\n<p>into an IP address.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3488-step-3-contact-the-server\">\n<h1>Step 3: Contact the Server</h1>\n<p>The browser sends a request.</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Client → Server </pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3488-step-4-routing\">\n<h1>Step 4: Routing</h1>\n<p>Packets travel through multiple routers.</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Home Network \n     ↓ \n     Internet Provider \n     ↓ \n     Internet \n     ↓ \n     Web Server </pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3488-step-5-server-response\">\n<h1>Step 5: Server Response</h1>\n<p>The web server sends:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>HTML</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Images</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Scripts</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>back to the browser.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3488-step-6-browser-displays-the-page\">\n<h1>Step 6: Browser Displays the Page</h1>\n<p>The browser interprets the information and displays the website.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3488-remark\">\n<h1>Remark</h1>\n<p>This entire process often completes in less than a second.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"6133cfca2393bfc5b8ff239e54a3ed2470856f5140a1dcd43093ad5a07a906c4","markdown":"## Een Reis Door het Internet \n\nLaten we volgen wat er gebeurt wanneer een student het volgende bezoekt: \n\n```text\n     www.example.com \n```\n\n### Stap 1: Gebruiker voert adres in \n\nDe student typt: \n\n```text\n     www.example.com \n```\n\nin een browser. \n\n \n\n### Stap 2: DNS-opzoeking \n\nDNS vertaalt: \n\n```text\n     www.example.com \n```\n\nnaar een IP-adres. \n\n \n\n### Stap 3: Contact opnemen met de server \n\nDe browser stuurt een verzoek. \n\n```text\n     Client → Server \n```\n\n### Stap 4: Routering \n\nPakketten reizen door meerdere routers. \n\n```text\n     Home Network \n     ↓ \n     Internet Provider \n     ↓ \n     Internet \n     ↓ \n     Web Server \n```\n\n### Stap 5: Reactie van de server \n\nDe webserver stuurt: \n\n- HTML \n\n- Afbeeldingen \n\n- Scripts \n\nterug naar de browser. \n\n### Stap 6: Browser toont de pagina \n\nDe browser interpreteert de informatie en toont de website. \n\n \n\n### Opmerking \n\nDit hele proces wordt vaak in minder dan een seconde voltooid. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"6133cfca2393bfc5b8ff239e54a3ed2470856f5140a1dcd43093ad5a07a906c4","markdown":"## Un voyage à travers Internet\n\nSuivons ce qui se passe lorsqu'un étudiant visite :\n\n```text\n     www.example.com \n```\n\n### Étape 1 : L'utilisateur saisit l'adresse\n\nL'étudiant tape :\n\n```text\n     www.example.com \n```\n\ndans un navigateur.\n\n\n\n### Étape 2 : Recherche DNS\n\nLe DNS traduit :\n\n```text\n     www.example.com \n```\n\nen une adresse IP.\n\n\n\n### Étape 3 : Contacter le serveur\n\nLe navigateur envoie une requête.\n\n```text\n     Client → Server \n```\n\n### Étape 4 : Routage\n\nLes paquets traversent plusieurs routeurs.\n\n```text\n     Home Network \n     ↓ \n     Internet Provider \n     ↓ \n     Internet \n     ↓ \n     Web Server \n```\n\n### Étape 5 : Réponse du serveur\n\nLe serveur web renvoie :\n\n- HTML\n\n- Images\n\n- Scripts\n\nau navigateur.\n\n### Étape 6 : Le navigateur affiche la page\n\nLe navigateur interprète les informations et affiche le site web.\n\n\n\n### Remarque\n\nTout ce processus se termine souvent en moins d'une seconde."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"6133cfca2393bfc5b8ff239e54a3ed2470856f5140a1dcd43093ad5a07a906c4","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Other Internet Services \n\nThe Internet supports much more than websites. \n\n \n\n### Email \n\nAllows asynchronous communication. \n\n \n\n### Video Streaming \n\nExamples: \n\n- YouTube \n\n- Netflix \n\n \n\n### Voice and Video Communication \n\nExamples: \n\n- Teams \n\n- Zoom \n\n- WhatsApp \n\n \n\n### Online Gaming \n\nConnects players worldwide. \n\n \n\n### Artificial Intelligence Services \n\nMany AI applications operate on remote servers and are accessed through the Internet. ","output":"","result":"## Other Internet Services \n\nThe Internet supports much more than websites. \n\n \n\n### Email \n\nAllows asynchronous communication. \n\n \n\n### Video Streaming \n\nExamples: \n\n- YouTube \n\n- Netflix \n\n \n\n### Voice and Video Communication \n\nExamples: \n\n- Teams \n\n- Zoom \n\n- WhatsApp \n\n \n\n### Online Gaming \n\nConnects players worldwide. \n\n \n\n### Artificial Intelligence Services \n\nMany AI applications operate on remote servers and are accessed through the Internet. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3489-other-internet-services\">\n<h1>Other Internet Services</h1>\n<p>The Internet supports much more than websites.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3489-email\">\n<h1>Email</h1>\n<p>Allows asynchronous communication.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3489-video-streaming\">\n<h1>Video Streaming</h1>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>YouTube</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Netflix</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3489-voice-and-video-communication\">\n<h1>Voice and Video Communication</h1>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Teams</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Zoom</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>WhatsApp</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3489-online-gaming\">\n<h1>Online Gaming</h1>\n<p>Connects players worldwide.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3489-artificial-intelligence-services\">\n<h1>Artificial Intelligence Services</h1>\n<p>Many AI applications operate on remote servers and are accessed through the Internet.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"02f2b8a1124410ba09c56d78321cd69005c863a275ef73d71f8513c75ae4eab6","markdown":"## Andere Internetdiensten \n\nHet internet biedt veel meer dan websites. \n\n \n\n### E-mail \n\nMaakt asynchrone communicatie mogelijk. \n\n \n\n### Videostreaming \n\nVoorbeelden: \n\n- YouTube \n\n- Netflix \n\n \n\n### Spraak- en videocommunicatie \n\nVoorbeelden: \n\n- Teams \n\n- Zoom \n\n- WhatsApp \n\n \n\n### Online gamen \n\nVerbindt spelers wereldwijd. \n\n \n\n### Diensten voor kunstmatige intelligentie \n\nVeel AI-toepassingen draaien op externe servers en worden benaderd via het internet. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"02f2b8a1124410ba09c56d78321cd69005c863a275ef73d71f8513c75ae4eab6","markdown":"## Autres services Internet \n\nInternet prend en charge bien plus que des sites web. \n\n \n\n### Courrier électronique \n\nPermet une communication asynchrone. \n\n \n\n### Diffusion vidéo en continu \n\nExemples : \n\n- YouTube \n\n- Netflix \n\n \n\n### Communication vocale et vidéo \n\nExemples : \n\n- Teams \n\n- Zoom \n\n- WhatsApp \n\n \n\n### Jeux en ligne \n\nConnecte des joueurs du monde entier. \n\n \n\n### Services d'intelligence artificielle \n\nDe nombreuses applications d'IA fonctionnent sur des serveurs distants et sont accessibles via Internet. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"02f2b8a1124410ba09c56d78321cd69005c863a275ef73d71f8513c75ae4eab6","language":"English"}},{"input":"### Summary \n\nIn this chapter we learned: \n\n- Networks connect computers and other devices. \n\n- The Internet is a global network of networks. \n\n- Protocols define communication rules. \n\n- Information is transmitted using packets. \n\n- IP addresses identify devices. \n\n- DNS translates domain names into IP addresses. \n\n- The client-server model underlies many Internet services. \n\n- IP handles addressing and routing. \n\n- TCP provides reliable communication. \n\n- UDP prioritizes speed over reliability. \n\n- Routers forward packets across networks. \n\n- The World Wide Web is a service built on top of the Internet. \n\n- Browsers and servers cooperate to provide web content. \n\n- Cloud computing uses remote servers to provide services. \n\n- Visiting a website involves many coordinated steps. ","output":"","result":"### Summary \n\nIn this chapter we learned: \n\n- Networks connect computers and other devices. \n\n- The Internet is a global network of networks. \n\n- Protocols define communication rules. \n\n- Information is transmitted using packets. \n\n- IP addresses identify devices. \n\n- DNS translates domain names into IP addresses. \n\n- The client-server model underlies many Internet services. \n\n- IP handles addressing and routing. \n\n- TCP provides reliable communication. \n\n- UDP prioritizes speed over reliability. \n\n- Routers forward packets across networks. \n\n- The World Wide Web is a service built on top of the Internet. \n\n- Browsers and servers cooperate to provide web content. \n\n- Cloud computing uses remote servers to provide services. \n\n- Visiting a website involves many coordinated steps. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3490-summary\">\n<h1>Summary</h1>\n<p>In this chapter we learned:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Networks connect computers and other devices.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The Internet is a global network of networks.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Protocols define communication rules.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Information is transmitted using packets.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>IP addresses identify devices.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>DNS translates domain names into IP addresses.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The client-server model underlies many Internet services.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>IP handles addressing and routing.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>TCP provides reliable communication.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>UDP prioritizes speed over reliability.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Routers forward packets across networks.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The World Wide Web is a service built on top of the Internet.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Browsers and servers cooperate to provide web content.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Cloud computing uses remote servers to provide services.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Visiting a website involves many coordinated steps.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"1872765d7d04a47eb3b2c823dd7f881cc3bd76a31c9dacb455debcc31014a87c","markdown":"### Samenvatting\n\nIn dit hoofdstuk hebben we geleerd dat: \n\n- Netwerken computers en andere apparaten met elkaar verbinden. \n\n- Het internet een wereldwijd netwerk van netwerken is. \n\n- Protocollen de regels voor communicatie bepalen. \n\n- Informatie wordt verzonden met behulp van pakketten. \n\n- IP-adressen apparaten identificeren. \n\n- DNS domeinnamen vertaalt naar IP-adressen. \n\n- Het client-servermodel aan de basis ligt van veel internetdiensten. \n\n- IP zorgt voor adressering en routering. \n\n- TCP betrouwbare communicatie biedt. \n\n- UDP snelheid boven betrouwbaarheid stelt. \n\n- Routers pakketten doorsturen tussen netwerken. \n\n- Het World Wide Web een dienst is die bovenop het internet is gebouwd. \n\n- Browsers en servers samenwerken om webinhoud te leveren. \n\n- Cloud computing externe servers gebruikt om diensten te leveren. \n\n- Het bezoeken van een website veel gecoördineerde stappen omvat."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"1872765d7d04a47eb3b2c823dd7f881cc3bd76a31c9dacb455debcc31014a87c","markdown":"### Résumé\n\nDans ce chapitre, nous avons appris que :\n\n- Les réseaux connectent des ordinateurs et d'autres appareils.\n\n- Internet est un réseau mondial de réseaux.\n\n- Les protocoles définissent les règles de communication.\n\n- L'information est transmise à l'aide de paquets.\n\n- Les adresses IP identifient les appareils.\n\n- Le DNS traduit les noms de domaine en adresses IP.\n\n- Le modèle client-serveur est à la base de nombreux services Internet.\n\n- IP gère l'adressage et le routage.\n\n- TCP fournit une communication fiable.\n\n- UDP privilégie la vitesse plutôt que la fiabilité.\n\n- Les routeurs transmettent les paquets à travers les réseaux.\n\n- Le World Wide Web est un service construit au-dessus d'Internet.\n\n- Les navigateurs et les serveurs coopèrent pour fournir du contenu web.\n\n- L'informatique en nuage utilise des serveurs distants pour fournir des services.\n\n- Visiter un site web implique de nombreuses étapes coordonnées."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"1872765d7d04a47eb3b2c823dd7f881cc3bd76a31c9dacb455debcc31014a87c","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Key Terms \n\n{.wide}\n|Term | Definition| \n|:----|:----------|\n|Network|Collection of devices capable of communication|\n|LAN |Local Area Network |\n|Internet |Global network of interconnected networks |\n|Protocol |Rules governing communication |\n|Packet |Unit of data transmitted across a network |\n|IP Address |Numerical identifier of a device |\n|Domain Name |Human-readable Internet address |\n|DNS |System translating names into IP addresses |\n|Client |Device or application requesting a service |\n|Server |Device providing a service |\n|IP |Internet Protocol |\n|TCP |Reliable transport protocol |\n|UDP |Lightweight transport protocol |\n|Router |Device forwarding packets between networks |\n|Web Browser |Application used to access web content |\n|Web Server |Server providing websites |\n|Cloud Computing |Delivery of services from remote systems |\n\n","output":"","result":"## Key Terms \n\n{.wide}\n|Term | Definition| \n|:----|:----------|\n|Network|Collection of devices capable of communication|\n|LAN |Local Area Network |\n|Internet |Global network of interconnected networks |\n|Protocol |Rules governing communication |\n|Packet |Unit of data transmitted across a network |\n|IP Address |Numerical identifier of a device |\n|Domain Name |Human-readable Internet address |\n|DNS |System translating names into IP addresses |\n|Client |Device or application requesting a service |\n|Server |Device providing a service |\n|IP |Internet Protocol |\n|TCP |Reliable transport protocol |\n|UDP |Lightweight transport protocol |\n|Router |Device forwarding packets between networks |\n|Web Browser |Application used to access web content |\n|Web Server |Server providing websites |\n|Cloud Computing |Delivery of services from remote systems |\n\n","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3491-key-terms\">\n<h1>Key Terms</h1>\n<figure data-type=\"table\" class=\"wide\">\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"left\">Term</th>\n<th class=\"left\">Definition</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">Network</td>\n<td class=\"left\">Collection of devices capable of communication</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">LAN</td>\n<td class=\"left\">Local Area Network</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">Internet</td>\n<td class=\"left\">Global network of interconnected networks</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">Protocol</td>\n<td class=\"left\">Rules governing communication</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">Packet</td>\n<td class=\"left\">Unit of data transmitted across a network</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">IP Address</td>\n<td class=\"left\">Numerical identifier of a device</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">Domain Name</td>\n<td class=\"left\">Human-readable Internet address</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">DNS</td>\n<td class=\"left\">System translating names into IP addresses</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">Client</td>\n<td class=\"left\">Device or application requesting a service</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">Server</td>\n<td class=\"left\">Device providing a service</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">IP</td>\n<td class=\"left\">Internet Protocol</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">TCP</td>\n<td class=\"left\">Reliable transport protocol</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">UDP</td>\n<td class=\"left\">Lightweight transport protocol</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">Router</td>\n<td class=\"left\">Device forwarding packets between networks</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">Web Browser</td>\n<td class=\"left\">Application used to access web content</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">Web Server</td>\n<td class=\"left\">Server providing websites</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"left\">Cloud Computing</td>\n<td class=\"left\">Delivery of services from remote systems</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</figure>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"c752704675da72710206759b4834798d7e92f09a08cd510d36abaa0ee622ec1c","markdown":"## Kernbegrippen\n\n{.wide}\n|Term | Definitie|\n|:----|:----------|\n|Netwerk|Verzameling van apparaten die met elkaar kunnen communiceren|\n|LAN |Lokaal netwerk |\n|Internet |Wereldwijd netwerk van onderling verbonden netwerken |\n|Protocol |Regels die communicatie bepalen |\n|Pakket |Eenheid van gegevens die over een netwerk wordt verzonden |\n|IP-adres |Numerieke identificatie van een apparaat |\n|Domeinnaam |Door mensen leesbaar internetadres |\n|DNS |Systeem dat namen vertaalt naar IP-adressen |\n|Client |Apparaat of toepassing dat een dienst aanvraagt |\n|Server |Apparaat dat een dienst levert |\n|IP |Internet Protocol |\n|TCP |Betrouwbaar transportprotocol |\n|UDP |Lichtgewicht transportprotocol |\n|Router |Apparaat dat pakketten tussen netwerken doorstuurt |\n|Webbrowser |Toepassing om webinhoud te openen |\n|Webserver |Server die websites levert |\n|Cloud computing |Levering van diensten vanaf externe systemen |\n"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"c752704675da72710206759b4834798d7e92f09a08cd510d36abaa0ee622ec1c","markdown":"## Termes clés\n\n{.wide}\n|Terme | Définition|\n|:----|:----------|\n|Réseau|Ensemble d'appareils capables de communiquer|\n|LAN |Réseau local |\n|Internet |Réseau mondial de réseaux interconnectés |\n|Protocole |Règles régissant la communication |\n|Paquet |Unité de données transmise sur un réseau |\n|Adresse IP |Identifiant numérique d'un appareil |\n|Nom de domaine |Adresse Internet lisible par l'humain |\n|DNS |Système traduisant les noms en adresses IP |\n|Client |Appareil ou application demandant un service |\n|Serveur |Appareil fournissant un service |\n|IP |Protocole Internet |\n|TCP |Protocole de transport fiable |\n|UDP |Protocole de transport léger |\n|Routeur |Appareil acheminant les paquets entre réseaux |\n|Navigateur Web |Application utilisée pour accéder au contenu web |\n|Serveur Web |Serveur fournissant des sites web |\n|Informatique en nuage |Fourniture de services depuis des systèmes distants |\n"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"c752704675da72710206759b4834798d7e92f09a08cd510d36abaa0ee622ec1c","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Review Questions \n\n- What is a computer network? \n\n- What is the difference between a LAN and the Internet? \n\n- Why do networks require protocols? \n\n- What is a packet? \n\n- Why are IP addresses necessary? \n\n- What problem does DNS solve? \n\n- What is the difference between a client and a server? \n\n- What is the role of IP? \n\n- Why does TCP exist if IP already provides communication? \n\n- When might UDP be preferred over TCP? \n\n- What does a router do? \n\n- What is the difference between the Internet and the World Wide Web? \n\n- What is cloud computing? \n\n- Describe the complete journey of a web request from browser to server and back. ","output":"","result":"## Review Questions \n\n- What is a computer network? \n\n- What is the difference between a LAN and the Internet? \n\n- Why do networks require protocols? \n\n- What is a packet? \n\n- Why are IP addresses necessary? \n\n- What problem does DNS solve? \n\n- What is the difference between a client and a server? \n\n- What is the role of IP? \n\n- Why does TCP exist if IP already provides communication? \n\n- When might UDP be preferred over TCP? \n\n- What does a router do? \n\n- What is the difference between the Internet and the World Wide Web? \n\n- What is cloud computing? \n\n- Describe the complete journey of a web request from browser to server and back. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3492-review-questions\">\n<h1>Review Questions</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>What is a computer network?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What is the difference between a LAN and the Internet?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Why do networks require protocols?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What is a packet?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Why are IP addresses necessary?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What problem does DNS solve?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What is the difference between a client and a server?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What is the role of IP?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Why does TCP exist if IP already provides communication?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>When might UDP be preferred over TCP?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What does a router do?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What is the difference between the Internet and the World Wide Web?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What is cloud computing?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Describe the complete journey of a web request from browser to server and back.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"ff964bff4df716df805e1e6d1d41d5eed2105a14bbadc227af6d28fc4363ab16","markdown":"## Herhalingsvragen\n\n- Wat is een computernetwerk?\n\n- Wat is het verschil tussen een LAN en het internet?\n\n- Waarom hebben netwerken protocollen nodig?\n\n- Wat is een pakket?\n\n- Waarom zijn IP-adressen noodzakelijk?\n\n- Welk probleem lost DNS op?\n\n- Wat is het verschil tussen een client en een server?\n\n- Wat is de rol van IP?\n\n- Waarom bestaat TCP als IP al communicatie mogelijk maakt?\n\n- Wanneer zou UDP de voorkeur hebben boven TCP?\n\n- Wat doet een router?\n\n- Wat is het verschil tussen het internet en het World Wide Web?\n\n- Wat is cloud computing?\n\n- Beschrijf de volledige reis van een webverzoek van browser naar server en terug."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"ff964bff4df716df805e1e6d1d41d5eed2105a14bbadc227af6d28fc4363ab16","markdown":"## Questions de révision\n\n- Qu'est-ce qu'un réseau informatique ?\n\n- Quelle est la différence entre un réseau local (LAN) et Internet ?\n\n- Pourquoi les réseaux nécessitent-ils des protocoles ?\n\n- Qu'est-ce qu'un paquet ?\n\n- Pourquoi les adresses IP sont-elles nécessaires ?\n\n- Quel problème le DNS résout-il ?\n\n- Quelle est la différence entre un client et un serveur ?\n\n- Quel est le rôle d'IP ?\n\n- Pourquoi TCP existe-t-il alors qu'IP assure déjà la communication ?\n\n- Quand UDP pourrait-il être préféré à TCP ?\n\n- Que fait un routeur ?\n\n- Quelle est la différence entre Internet et le World Wide Web ?\n\n- Qu'est-ce que l'informatique en nuage (cloud computing) ?\n\n- Décrivez le trajet complet d'une requête web, du navigateur au serveur et retour."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"ff964bff4df716df805e1e6d1d41d5eed2105a14bbadc227af6d28fc4363ab16","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Transition to Lecture 9 \n\nThe Internet has connected billions of devices and made information accessible worldwide. However, connectivity also introduces risks. Systems can be attacked, data can be stolen, and users can be deceived. \n\nIn the next lecture, we will study **Cybersecurity** and **Cryptography**, learning how digital systems are protected and how trust is established in an interconnected world. ","output":"","result":"## Transition to Lecture 9 \n\nThe Internet has connected billions of devices and made information accessible worldwide. However, connectivity also introduces risks. Systems can be attacked, data can be stolen, and users can be deceived. \n\nIn the next lecture, we will study **Cybersecurity** and **Cryptography**, learning how digital systems are protected and how trust is established in an interconnected world. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture08-c3493-transition-to-lecture-9\">\n<h1>Transition to Lecture 9</h1>\n<p>The Internet has connected billions of devices and made information accessible worldwide. However, connectivity also introduces risks. Systems can be attacked, data can be stolen, and users can be deceived.</p>\n<p>In the next lecture, we will study <strong>Cybersecurity</strong> and <strong>Cryptography</strong>, learning how digital systems are protected and how trust is established in an interconnected world.</p>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"2d43dc6d0dc7bf2091e8e35c1a5cb1460b5ca245aba4fc706197a2221bbfb7de","markdown":"## Overgang naar Les 9 \n\nHet internet heeft miljarden apparaten met elkaar verbonden en informatie wereldwijd toegankelijk gemaakt. Connectiviteit brengt echter ook risico's met zich mee. Systemen kunnen worden aangevallen, gegevens kunnen worden gestolen en gebruikers kunnen worden misleid. \n\nIn de volgende les bestuderen we **Cyberbeveiliging** en **Cryptografie**, en leren we hoe digitale systemen worden beschermd en hoe vertrouwen tot stand komt in een onderling verbonden wereld. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"2d43dc6d0dc7bf2091e8e35c1a5cb1460b5ca245aba4fc706197a2221bbfb7de","markdown":"## Transition vers la leçon 9\n\nInternet a connecté des milliards d'appareils et a rendu l'information accessible dans le monde entier. Cependant, la connectivité introduit également des risques. Les systèmes peuvent être attaqués, les données peuvent être volées et les utilisateurs peuvent être trompés.\n\nDans la prochaine leçon, nous étudierons la **cybersécurité** et la **cryptographie**, en apprenant comment les systèmes numériques sont protégés et comment la confiance s'établit dans un monde interconnecté."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"2d43dc6d0dc7bf2091e8e35c1a5cb1460b5ca245aba4fc706197a2221bbfb7de","language":"English"}}]